"type":"text"},{"text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLAttributes","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAttributes"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAttributes"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes/staffDetails":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/staffdetails","fragments":[{"kind":"keywor